  "description": "A critical safety protocol implemented at the database level to prevent unsafe equipment from being put into service.",
  "definition": "A rule, typically enforced by a database trigger, that blocks any attempt to change an equipment's operational status to 'Active' if its current inspection status is 'Failed'. This ensures that equipment which has not passed safety checks cannot be used."
